 # reports
 
-`python3 reports.py < ledger.csv` prints `account,total_cents`, one row per
-account in alphabetical order, from the CSV that `ledger` exports.
+`python3 reports.py < ledger.csv` prints per-account totals, one row per
+(account, currency) pair, from the CSV that `ledger` exports.
+
+## Input
+
+CSV on stdin with the header `date,account,amount_cents,currency`, one
+transaction per row. `amount_cents` is an integer. `currency` is an ISO 4217
+code of exactly three uppercase ASCII letters, such as `EUR`.
+
+The old header `date,account,amount_cents` (no currency column) is also
+accepted; every row then counts as `USD`.
+
+A malformed currency code (for example `eur` or `EURO`) prints an error naming
+the input line to stderr and exits with status 2 without printing totals.
+
+## Output
+
+CSV on stdout with the header `account,currency,total_cents`. Each row is the
+sum of `amount_cents` for one account and currency. Rows are sorted by account,
+then by currency.
+
+```
+$ printf 'date,account,amount_cents,currency\n2026-03-01,rent,-120000,EUR\n2026-03-02,rent,-10,USD\n' | python3 reports.py
+account,currency,total_cents
+rent,EUR,-120000
+rent,USD,-10
+```
